            "channelId": "UCsT0YIqwnpJCM-mx7-gSA4Q",
            "videoId": "_VB39Jo8mAQ",
            "textDisplay": "Those who say earning money is more important than budgeting — I would like to point out that there are two important lessons about money: budgeting, which Adam talks about in the video, and earning, which people mention in the comments.\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003eI believe that if your kids are 7, 9, and 11, teaching them budgeting first is not a bad idea. Life — and you, as a parent — will teach them the other lessons as they grow into teenagers.\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003eA lot of adults only know one of these lessons and struggle because of it.\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003eI’ll definitely use some of the methods mentioned here to teach my 5- and 7-year-olds about money.",
            "textOriginal": "Those who say earning money is more important than budgeting — I would like to point out that there are two important lessons about money: budgeting, which Adam talks about in the video, and earning, which people mention in the comments.\n\nI believe that if your kids are 7, 9, and 11, teaching them budgeting first is not a bad idea. Life — and you, as a parent — will teach them the other lessons as they grow into teenagers.\n\nA lot of adults only know one of these lessons and struggle because of it.\n\nI’ll definitely use some of the methods mentioned here to teach my 5- and 7-year-olds about money.",
