          "snippet": {
            "channelId": "UCsT0YIqwnpJCM-mx7-gSA4Q",
            "videoId": "_VB39Jo8mAQ",
            "textDisplay": "I have to question this guys story of monopoly.. you always buy the properties early on it&#39;s very rare for someone to have setup hotels while there is still a sizable number of properties to be bought and a game that has not progressed to house/hotel development will go no practically forever as undeveloped property rent is very low and you get 200 every time you pass go.\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003eI once played with my nephew who got it in this head not to buy property he didn&#39;t like and save his money.. guess what it ended very bad for him esp if you play by the rules and auction it off if it&#39;s not bought by the landing player.\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003eI think he makes a good point about the reality of money but the monopoly story sounds like it&#39;s being misremembered or there are other details to that games rules he&#39;s forgetting to tell us.\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003eOr perhaps the kid wanted to save every dollar and so was worried to land on a property and pay out 20 bucks when he&#39;s sitting on 1k.\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003eIn which case the lesson of the reality of money takes a back seat to the much bigger lesson that should have been taught, that money is a tool, and nothing more.\u003cbr\u003eit&#39;s like energy stored in a battery, it is only useful when used, it&#39;s how it&#39;s used that is the important part.",
